  "coverage": "partial",
  "coverage_explanation": "Exercises two initial automatic cycles, automatic-mode independence from potentiometer changes, manual selection and five ADC levels including both endpoints, repeated manual selection, return to automatic operation, another automatic cycle, automatic reselection while already automatic, and a final return to manual operation. PWM ranges accommodate the permitted 500 ms initialization time or 250 ms button-response latency, as applicable, plus integer quantization. This is finite behavioral coverage, not proof for every ADC value or ramp instant.",
  "assumptions": [
    "The disclosed authoritative wiring is used: active-HIGH LED PWM on D9, potentiometer on A0, and active-LOW buttons D2/D3 connected to GND with INPUT_PULLUP.",
    "Manual ADC-to-PWM control uses the full linear ADC 0..1023 to PWM 0..255 conversion; a one-count tolerance permits integer rounding or truncation.",
    "The disclosed bench ramp is linear, lasts 2000 ms in each direction, and repeats without an additional endpoint hold.",
    "No simultaneous button presses are tested because button priority is unspecified.",
    "Automatic timing checks allow initialization anywhere within the authorized 500 ms startup limit. Button-triggered ramp checks allow selection latency from 0 through 250 ms.",
    "The reference optionally uses 20 ms press debouncing. The tests do not require that particular debounce implementation."
  ],
